{"_v":1,"id":"the-book-of-mormon-west-end-2024","bd":{"positive":6,"mixed":0,"negative":1},"rv":[{"cn":"Allis Brennan","o":"Evening Standard","s":95,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/go/london/theatre/the-book-of-mormon-musical-theatre-tickets-in-london-a3706421.html","d":"2017-11-20","q":"If you believe in a perfect musical, this might just be it."},{"cn":"JeanPierre 4251","o":"The Times (UK)","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.show-score.com/uk/london/west-end-shows/the-book-of-mormon-london","q":"A night of unalloyed joy. And damned fine music."},{"cn":"Euan Ferguson","o":"The Guardian","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2013/mar/24/book-of-mormon-review","d":"2013-03-24","q":"The Book of Mormon is far, far cleverer, far kinder, far more nuanced than that, and one of its many surprises is that it sent an enraptured, ecstatic audience home with an odd sense of having come, somehow, to really like Mormons."},{"cn":"Charles Spencer","o":"The Telegraph","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/theatre/theatre-reviews/9946475/The-Book-of-Mormon-Prince-of-Wales-Theatre-review.html","d":"2013-03-22","q":"And yet, the sneaky truth is that this wild, thrilling, go-for-broke, genuinely hilarious musical comedy remains one of the funniest shows in the West End."},{"cn":"Libby Purves","o":"The Times (UK)","s":45,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/the-book-of-mormon-prince-of-wales-w1-28gmrq88q5l","d":"2013-03-22","q":"It offers big belting numbers, witty lyrics, and joyfully athletic dances."},{"cn":"Paul Taylor","o":"The Independent","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/theatre-review-the-book-of-mormon-merely-flirts-with-blasphemy-but-there-is-something-very-winning-8543751.html","d":"2013-03-21","q":"Directed with terrific zap and zestful precision."},{"cn":"Ian Shuttleworth","o":"Financial Times","s":74,